no-wifi.patch: pair this iPhone with Wi-Fi off.

Applies to FrizzleM/SideInstaller (ios-app/). Wi-Fi was only needed so that
Settings > Privacy & Security > Developer Mode could find SideInstaller over
Bonjour for the one-time pairing; the install itself runs over LocalDevVPN.

- Install no longer stops, or waits, for Wi-Fi; the "Wi-Fi required" card is gone.
- When Wi-Fi is off at the start of a pairing, the pairing service is
  registered with dns_sd on kDNSServiceInterfaceIndexLocalOnly (visible only
  to clients on this iPhone, such as Settings) with localhost as its target,
  and the listener binds to :: so it answers on 127.0.0.1 and ::1.
- With Wi-Fi off the Local Network check can't see its own probe, so it
  counts silence as granted; an explicit denial still stops the run.
- With Wi-Fi on, nothing changes. Side by Side still needs Wi-Fi.

Unverified on a device: whether Settings lists a host advertised this way.

